  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The method is not reproducible yet: tau, the alpha grid, residual scaling, empty-history handling, and global versus category-specific weight selection are unspecified.",
    "For an unobserved transition from an observed source, the residual equals -n_i*p(j)/(n_i+tau). This introduces a source-frequency-dependent popularity penalty that needs a separate control.",
    "The diagnostic scoring contract lacks sequence context for the transition branch. Unless adapted, predict_score(features, items) may diagnose SASRec alone while the deployed predictor uses combined scores.",
    "The potential score of 8 lacks experimental support. Sparse transition coverage, validation-search overfitting, and the contribution beyond popularity correction remain unmeasured."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Determine whether improvements would reflect useful transition information or primarily a popularity penalty, and identify appropriate alternative baselines.",
      "query": "In sequential recommendation, how do additive transition models using r(i,j)=(C[i,j]+tau*p(j))/(n_i+tau)-p(j) compare with popularity-only score correction, conditional log-lift, and history-aware item-item models? Examine sparse-transition coverage, source-frequency effects, and ablations that isolate transition information from popularity debiasing."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Resolve implementation details needed for reproducible scoring and architecture-aware diagnostics.",
      "query": "How should a SASRec plus sparse last-item transition ensemble implement training-only score normalization, smoothing strength, empty-history fallbacks, and efficient candidate/full-catalog scoring? Describe how per-position diagnostic scoring can receive the corresponding source item so diagnostic and deployed ensemble scores agree."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Specify a small, defensible validation search and distinguish exploratory gains from selection noise.",
      "query": "For recommender ensemble tuning with four equally weighted datasets, 200 fixed validation users per dataset, and 99 fixed negative candidates per user, what limited hyperparameter-search and paired uncertainty protocol is appropriate? Compare shared versus per-dataset ensemble weights and explain why a paired bootstrap after selecting the best configuration does not correct validation-selection optimism."
    }
  ]
}
